  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the best configuration (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), clearly above singleprofile PCA and multiprofile transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. This suggests the promising direction is multiprofile avgpool RNA modeling, but the RNA representation choice remains untested beyond PCA. config_008 keeps the proven multiprofile avgpool setting and changes only the RNA encoder to scgpt, directly testing whether a stronger learned RNA representation improves on PCA. This is a single-factor extension of the current best configuration, has high expected value if scgpt helps, and clarifies whether representation is the main remaining RNA lever before investing in multimodal fusion."
}

